---
/**
 * Track 8 (Visual Math: Calculus), Lesson 5, illustration 1 of 2.
 *
 * The product f(x)·g(x) as a rectangle. With f(x) = 3 and g(x) = 2 the
 * picture is a 3 by 2 box; the area equals the product. This is the
 * setup the product rule (next diagram) extends by growing both sides.
 */

const cx = 230;
const cy = 270;
const SCALE = 70;

const f = 3;
const g = 2;

const TEAL = '#0d9488';
const AMBER = '#d97706';
const ACCENT = '#7c3aed';
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 740 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="ca-prodrect-title ca-prodrect-desc">
		<title id="ca-prodrect-title">The product f(x) times g(x) as a rectangle of width f(x) and height g(x)</title>
		<desc id="ca-prodrect-desc">A rectangle drawn on a 2D scene. The width is labeled f of x, equal to 3, in teal along the bottom; the height is labeled g of x, equal to 2, in amber along the left side. The interior is filled lightly in accent purple and labeled at its center as f of x times g of x equals 6. This is the basic product-as-area visual that the product rule extends.</desc>

		{/* coordinate hint (very faint axes) */}
		<line x1={cx - 20} y1={cy} x2={cx + f * SCALE + 30} y2={cy} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.35" />
		<line x1={cx} y1={cy + 20} x2={cx} y2={cy - g * SCALE - 30} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.35" />

		{/* the rectangle */}
		<rect x={cx} y={cy - g * SCALE} width={f * SCALE} height={g * SCALE} fill={ACCENT} fill-opacity="0.18" stroke={ACCENT} stroke-width="1.8" />

		{/* center label: f·g */}
		<text x={cx + (f * SCALE) / 2} y={cy - (g * SCALE) / 2 - 6} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="22" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>f(x) · g(x)</text>
		<text x={cx + (f * SCALE) / 2} y={cy - (g * SCALE) / 2 + 22} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>= {f * g}</text>

		{/* dimension brackets */}
		<line x1={cx} y1={cy + 14} x2={cx + f * SCALE} y2={cy + 14} stroke={TEAL} stroke-width="1.4" />
		<line x1={cx} y1={cy + 10} x2={cx} y2={cy + 20} stroke={TEAL} stroke-width="1.4" />
		<line x1={cx + f * SCALE} y1={cy + 10} x2={cx + f * SCALE} y2={cy + 20} stroke={TEAL} stroke-width="1.4" />
		<text x={cx + (f * SCALE) / 2} y={cy + 32} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill={TEAL}>f(x) = {f}</text>

		<line x1={cx - 14} y1={cy} x2={cx - 14} y2={cy - g * SCALE} stroke={AMBER} stroke-width="1.4" />
		<line x1={cx - 10} y1={cy} x2={cx - 20} y2={cy} stroke={AMBER} stroke-width="1.4" />
		<line x1={cx - 10} y1={cy - g * SCALE} x2={cx - 20} y2={cy - g * SCALE} stroke={AMBER} stroke-width="1.4" />
		<text x={cx - 22} y={cy - (g * SCALE) / 2 + 4} text-anchor="end" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill={AMBER}>g(x) = {g}</text>

		{/* legend */}
		<g transform="translate(490, 130)">
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="220" height="100" rx="6" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.04" />
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="220" height="100" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.3" />
			<text x="110" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">product as rectangle area:</text>
			<text x="110" y="50" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>area = f(x) · g(x)</text>
			<text x="110" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6">next: grow f and g a little</text>
		</g>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>Two values multiplied is a rectangle: width f(x), height g(x), area f(x) times g(x). When f or g changes, that rectangle reshapes; tracking what gets added gives the product rule, the topic of the next picture.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 740px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
